nd controlling the center.\n\nHowever, **B: f8-b4** creates immediate tactical pressure and is a more forcing move.\n\nReason: Developing the bishop to b4 actively challenges White's setup, puts my pieces into play, maintains castling rights, and creates threats. This is more forcing than passive pawn moves and better than the alternatives like f8-c5 which, while decent, doesn't create as much immediate pressure.\n\nAnswer: B: f8-b4"}
