ition and fights for central control\n- After exd5, my rook would have an open file with targets\n\n**Reason:** Opening the center with d7-d5 creates immediate central tension and activates my rook on d8. This puts pressure on White's position, particularly the queen on d2 which must respond to the pawn advance. The move fights for central control and creates tactical opportunities.\n\n**Answer:** P: d7-d5"}
